Python data structures: lists, tuples, sets, and dictionaries. 

Lists
You can access list elements using their index. Remember, Python uses zero-based indexing
Lists are mutable, meaning you can change their contents
You can add items to a list using the append() method or insert items at a specific position using the insert() method
To remove items, you can use the remove() method or the del statement
Lists can contain items of different types, including other lists.

Understanding Tuples
Tuples are created using parentheses ().
tuples, which are ordered, immutable sequences in Python.
