Tuple unpacking is a convenient way to assign multiple variables at once.

Exploring Sets
Sets are created using curly braces {} or the set() function. Note that the order of elements may vary when you print a set.
You can add elements to a set using the add() method
Sets support mathematical set operations like union, intersection, and difference.
You can check if an element is in a set using the in keyword.

Working with Dictionaries
Dictionaries are created using curly braces {} with key-value pairs separated by colons :.
Dictionaries have useful methods like keys(), values(), and items().
